    {
      "anchor": "/home/ITER/mcintos/Code/reckon/docs/plans/the-monitor-shows-the-work-it-watches.html:743",
      "id": "reasoning-1",
      "reason": "a node confined to ticker.py cannot make `q` report 4, so it would either edit an unlisted file or fail its own first case; the write paths must add `reckon/crew/recovery_watch.py`.",
      "text": "\u00a7100's deliverable makes the `q` cell count every parked phase, but that number comes from `_fleet_counts` (`reckon/crew/recovery_watch.py:1395-1437`), where `WAITING_STATES` is `frozenset({\"waiting\", \"wait-aged\", \"paused\", \"queued\"})` (line 58) plus a separate `held` addend; `awaiting-upstream` and `blocked-upstream` fall into none of the working/blocked/unpromoted/waiting buckets. \u00a7100's write paths name only `reckon/crew/ticker.py` and the new test, and `ticker.py` only reads the event's count fields (`_stats`, line 3290)",
      "type": "reasoning",
      "would_change": true
    },
    {
      "anchor": "/home/ITER/mcintos/Code/reckon/docs/plans/the-monitor-shows-the-work-it-watches.html:743",
      "id": "done_when-1",
      "reason": "the worker must either drop the cell and break the invariant the module documents, or dim it and fail the case as written; the case has to say which.",
      "text": "the third case asserts \"a session with nothing stuck renders no `s` cell\", but the stat block's stated invariant is that every bucket renders on every row so the block never changes shape, with a zero dimmed rather than dropped (`reckon/crew/ticker.py:3276-3285`); \u00a7100 also keeps a width bound in the same clause",
      "type": "done_when",
      "would_change": true
    },
    {
      "anchor": "/home/ITER/mcintos/Code/reckon/docs/plans/the-monitor-shows-the-work-it-watches.html:747",
      "id": "reasoning-2",
      "reason": "\u00a7101 lands first and cannot satisfy its own gate, so the worker either edits an unlisted file or weakens the ticker clause; the ticker write path or the dependency direction has to move.",
      "text": "\u00a7101 requires \"the stop hook, `crew view live`, the drain view and the ticker\" to read the shared verdict and \"show its reason\", and its done-when makes the ticker's agreement part of the gate, but its write paths list only `runs.py`, `obligation_snapshot.py`, `recovery_classification.py` and the new test. The `s` cell and any reason row in the pane belong to \u00a7100, which declares `depends-on: s101` and is therefore admitted after \u00a7101",
      "type": "reasoning",
      "would_change": true
    },
    {
      "anchor": "/home/ITER/mcintos/Code/reckon/docs/plans/the-monitor-shows-the-work-it-watches.html:743",
      "id": "reasoning-3",
      "reason": "the deliverable already names all four parked phases, so the node's change is the same; the Why understates the defect without redirecting the work.",
      "text": "the Why says the waiting cell \"already counts queued runs and runs waiting on a declared condition\", implying the \u00a719 request was visible in `q` and only its stuck-ness was missing; the actual derivation counts `{waiting, wait-aged, paused, queued}` plus `held`, so the `awaiting-upstream` request that sat for 3 h was counted in no cell at all (`reckon/crew/recovery_watch.py:58` and `:1395-1437`)",
      "type": "reasoning",
      "would_change": false
    },
    {
      "anchor": "/home/ITER/mcintos/Code/reckon/docs/plans/the-monitor-shows-the-work-it-watches.html:747",
      "id": "reasoning-4",
      "reason": "the repository's lazy-import idiom already resolves the same direction (`recovery_classification.py:145,200`, `ticker.py:1825`), so the mechanism still runs without changing the plan's design.",
      "text": "placing the one stuck verdict in `runs.py` puts the caller in `obligation_snapshot.py`, which `runs.py` imports at module scope (`reckon/crew/runs.py:48`), so the new call closes an import cycle",
      "type": "reasoning",
      "would_change": false
    }
  ],
